<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manduria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manduria is a town in the province of Taranto in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. In antiquity it was a Messapian town with massive triple walls, and in 338 BCE the Spartan king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archidamus-iii">Archidamus III</a>, fighting for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarentum">Taras</a>, was killed in battle beneath them. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> took it during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>, and the well described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliny-the-elder">Pliny the Elder</a> still survives there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manduria.jpg" alt="Manduria" width="320" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrea FIstetto · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manduria_Piazza_Garibaldi_2020.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
